  "tempo": 1.12,
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Flip a padlock over and there is a small",
      "start": 0.106,
      "end": 2.001
    },
    {
      "text": "hole in the bottom of it, which looks like",
      "start": 2.107,
      "end": 3.55
    },
    {
      "text": "an excellent way to let water into an expensive",
      "start": 3.586,
      "end": 5.819
    },
    {
      "text": "lock.",
      "start": 5.89,
      "end": 6.258
    },
    {
      "text": "It does the opposite.",
      "start": 6.41,
      "end": 7.161
    },
    {
      "text": "A padlock left outdoors collects moisture no",
      "start": 7.368,
      "end": 9.528
    },
    {
      "text": "matter what you do,",
      "start": 9.582,
      "end": 10.261
    },
    {
      "text": "from rain,",
      "start": 10.526,
      "end": 11.062
    },
    {
      "text": "from washing,",
      "start": 11.365,
      "end": 11.936
    },
    {
      "text": "from the air itself.",
      "start": 12.241,
      "end": 13.134
    },
    {
      "text": "Sealed shut,",
      "start": 13.497,
      "end": 14.033
    },
    {
      "text": "that water sits on steel springs and pins",
      "start": 14.181,
      "end": 16.342
    },
    {
      "text": "until they rust into a solid lump,",
      "start": 16.645,
      "end": 18.236
    },
    {
      "text": "or freeze there overnight.",
      "start": 18.439,
      "end": 19.562
    },
    {
      "text": "The hole lets it fall straight back out.",
      "start": 19.809,
      "end": 21.488
    },
    {
      "text": "It also gives you somewhere to put a drop",
      "start": 21.765,
      "end": 23.266
    },
    {
      "text": "of oil.",
      "start": 23.303,
      "end": 23.839
    }
  ],
